<title>HUNGARY: AIRPORT LJUBLJANA CARGO TRADE JAN-MAY - BY AIRLINE.</title>
<headline>AIRPORT LJUBLJANA CARGO TRADE JAN-MAY - BY AIRLINE.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo trade at Airport</p>
<p>Ljubljana in the January-to-May period in 1996 and 1995 appears</p>
<p>below by airline, according to data provided to Reuters by the</p>
<p>airport.</p>
<p> CARGO TRADE (in tonnes)     JAN-MAY 96  JAN-MAY 95  PCT CHANGE</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> ADRIA AIRWAYS			1,579.9     1,850.7	 -14.6</p>
<p> --exports			    1,078.0     1,246.7	 -13.5</p>
<p> --imports				501.9	 604.0	 -16.9</p>
<p> LUFTHANSA				671.6	 790.0	 -15.0</p>
<p> --exports				185.1	 303.8	 -39.1</p>
<p> --imports				486.5	 486.2	  +0.1</p>
<p> AIR FRANCE			     323.3	 243.1	 +33.0</p>
<p> --exports				267.6	 192.9	 +38.7</p>
<p> --imports				 55.7	  50.2	 +11.0</p>
<p> AUSTRIAN AIRLINES		    283.0	 302.9	  -6.6</p>
<p> --exports				 43.4	  48.8	 -11.1</p>
<p> --imports				239.6	 254.1	  -5.7</p>
<p> KLM ROYAL DUTCH AIRLINES	   261.7	 145.0	 +80.5</p>
<p> --exports				166.5	  50.5	+229.7</p>
<p> --imports				 95.2	  94.5	  +0.7</p>
<p> SWISSAIR				 146.6	  60.6	+141.9</p>
<p> --exports				 72.9	  30.3	+140.6</p>
<p> --imports				 73.7	  30.3	+143.2</p>
<p> DHL WORLDWIDE EXPRESS		119.1	 116.5	  +2.2</p>
<p> --exports				 57.5	  69.2	 -16.9</p>
<p> --imports				 61.6	  47.3	 +30.2</p>
<p> AEROFLOT				   5.2	 103.1	 -95.0</p>
<p> --exports				  1.4	 101.9	 -98.6</p>
<p> --imports				  3.8	   1.2	+216.7</p>
<p> UNITED PARCEL SERVICE		  0.2	   0.0	     -</p>
<p> --exports				  0.2	   0.0	     -</p>
<p> --imports				  0.0	   0.0	     -</p>
<p> AVIOIMPEX				  0.0	 206.4	-100.0</p>
<p> --exports				  0.0	 183.5	-100.0</p>
<p> --imports				  0.0	  22.9	-100.0</p>
<p> OTHERS				   351.0	 614.8	 -42.9</p>
<p> --exports				211.4	 288.4	 -26.7</p>
<p> --imports				139.6	 326.4	 -57.2</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> TOTAL				  3,741.6     4,433.1	 -15.6</p>
<p> --exports			    2,084.0     2,516.0	 -17.2</p>
<p> --imports			    1,657.6     1,917.1	 -13.5</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE - Cargo includes freight and mail. Due to rounding,</p>
<p>some data in this report differ fractionally when appearing in</p>
<p>other reports by Reuters.</p>
<p>Cargo trade at the airport totalled 10,499 tonnes in 1995.</p>
<p>The airport, officially named Aerodrom Ljubljana po</p>
<p>Brnik, is owned 55.69 percent by the Slovenian state, 16.34</p>
<p>percent by past and present airport employees, 10.25 percent by</p>
<p>holders of airport equity sold publicly, 8.86 percent by the</p>
<p>Slovenian Fund for Development, 4.43 percent by the Slovenian</p>
<p>State Indemnity Fund and 4.43 percent by the Slovenian State</p>
<p>Pension Fund.</p>
<p>-- Ryan Tutak, Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410</p>
